theory.intro:
A data display shows values you can read straight off it. To draw a conclusion, read the values the question asks about, then compare or combine them — the highest, the lowest, a difference, or a trend. A prediction assumes the observed pattern continues; the graph does not establish future values.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.6,0);
\foreach \v/\p in {10/1,20/2,30/3,40/4} {\draw (-0.2,\p)--(0,\p); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\p) {$\v$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\fill[blue!25,draw=black] (0.6,0) rectangle (1.6,2.5);
\fill[blue!25,draw=black] (2.0,0) rectangle (3.0,4.0);
\fill[blue!25,draw=black] (3.4,0) rectangle (4.4,1.2);
\fill[blue!25,draw=black] (4.8,0) rectangle (5.8,3.0);
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1.1,0) {$A$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2.5,0) {$B$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3.9,0) {$C$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (5.3,0) {$D$};
\draw[dashed] (0.6,2.5)--(-0.2,2.5);
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.25,2.5) {$v$};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-1.2,2.0) {Value};
\node[below,font=\small] at (3.2,-0.9) {Category};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (3.2,5.1) {Reading a column graph};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

facts:
A steady **trend** up or down can be used to **predict** the next value, assuming the observed pattern continues. A prediction is not a guaranteed future value.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.6,0);
\foreach \v/\p in {10/1,20/2,30/3,40/4} {\draw (-0.2,\p)--(0,\p); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\p) {$\v$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\foreach \t in {1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\t,-0.15)--(\t,0); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\t,-0.15) {$\t$};}
\draw[thick] (1,1)--(2,1.8)--(3,2.6)--(4,3.4);
\foreach \x/\y in {1/1,2/1.8,3/2.6,4/3.4} {\fill (\x,\y) circle (2pt);}
\draw[dashed] (4,3.4)--(5,4.2);
\draw (5,4.2) circle (2.5pt);
\node[right,font=\scriptsize] at (5.2,4.2) {predicted};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-1.2,2.0) {Value};
\node[below,font=\small] at (3.2,-0.9) {Time};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (3.2,5.1) {Continuing a steady trend};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

